Z||000015||Flamberge||10-26-2001||01:47 PM||||Master_Sushi you're right, Saabs are fast. I should have known better too, because a buddy off mine has a 9000 convertable. But the guy I raced was coming up on me quick and I danced on his grave, leaving him back four or five car lengths, but then we got to a light and he smoke-checked me.<P>Well, at least my car doesn't look like someone knocked over a refridgerator.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Voytek||10-26-2001||02:23 PM||||That's a cool kill.  My verdict's still out on the new Monte Carlos.<P>I ALMOST had a kill last night, does that count?  The conditions were absolutely perfect, too.  About 70% humidity and 3 deg below zero (I think that's about 28 deg F).<P>Anyways, I caught up with a late '80s MR2.  It was only a 2 lane road for a while.  He sees me catch up so he goes from about 60 kph (38 mph) to about 100 kph (60 mph), or about 30 kms over the speed limit.<P>So I think 'great, hopefully I can get him at a light'.  Well, what do you know.  The road changed to 4 lanes in no time and we pulled up sided by side at a red light.  It was a very nice white MR2 (1st gen).  The dude was about 22 yrs of age with his g/f.  They looked over at my car.  She was smilin' and said something to him.  They talked for a few seconds.<BR>Then the light changes.  He revvs it a bit and then PUSSIES OUT.  What a BUMMER!!  I was ready to put him in his place with my 3.1.  This would have made my night.  I peeled out for his g/f anyways.<P>I was just imagining the conversation they were having at the light: <BR>g/f: 'nice yellow car, what is it?'<BR>b/f: 'oh, it's just a Fiero'.<BR>g/f: 'A Fiero?  THAT looks NICE.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I think he wants to race you.  Are you going to take him?'<BR>b/f: 'Nah, I would but it's just too easy'<BR>OR, a more appropriate reply:  'Nah, he can probably beat the panties off me'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Either way, he chickened out and I was veeeery disappointed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroKyle||10-26-2001||03:06 PM||||Well, I love the looks of the brand new Monte SS. Yes they are fast. Not as fast as I wished it was, really needs the supercharged 3800. I have no doubt in my mind you beat one with your Fiero. They don't out run a stock Fiero GT by much, but they do a little. Got to know how to drive it right. I would go on and on about GM cars and how great they are, but may be I will save that when I get home from work in a few hours. Until then later.....<P>Kyle - 85 GT||||reg||1
Z||000018||Uaana||10-26-2001||03:15 PM||||Kyle. <BR>The 3.4 is out of a 95 Firebird. As far as H.P. numbers, no idea. We noticed when we had it apart (sent in the heads for a massage while we had the engine out) that the engine appeared to have been recently rebuilt. It could use a new chip to correct a minor fuel mgt problem, likes to hunt for idle. Only other current mod would be Cat delete.. As for installation.. piece of cake. Dropped it off at a Very Trustworty mechanic bug him every couple of days and pickup in a month or so.. Never hassle your mechanic when he is cutting you a deal!||||reg||1
Z||000019||BlackStang95||10-26-2001||04:53 PM||||The 95 3.4's made 170 hp i think||||reg||1
Z||000020||88formula||10-26-2001||05:31 PM||||They made 160 horsepower.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
